## Failure analysis and limitations

Current paired model-forward medians are approximately24.79ms for CPU TieredKV and25.11ms for SnapKV. CPU required policy work adds approximately29.80ms/token. An exact instrumented replay attributes work across scoring, visibility, transfers and per-layer state updates. Cold-library initialization and resource observers contaminate aggregate profile totals; nested cumulative costs overlap. They rank engineering hypotheses and do not predict additive savings.

The latency primary and p95 guard fail. The early-shared candidate remains a recorded component result; candidate expansion/adoption stops under the preregistered protocol. No favorable retry or consumed final-holdout tuning is permitted. Existing development parity cannot establish unseen task quality. Historical DirectCPU independent quality failed non-inferiority and is not a current-candidate quality result. Physical controller pages, amplification, energy/endurance, broader model/seed/concurrency results and fair multi-request FlexiCache/IceCache comparisons remain unproved.

